ieve the effect of multimedia, can also play a time-saving role." So, the main point is that using courseware can save time, even if it\'s too simple. So, the hypothesis is that using courseware can save time, which is D.\n\nBut the argument is that using courseware can improve teaching effects, which is the main premise. However, the options don\'t have that as a separate option. So, perhaps the correct answer is D because it\'s the specific benefit mentioned, which is the hypothesis.\n\nWait, no. The argument is that using courseware can improve effects, and even if it\'s too simple, it can save time. So, the hypothesis is that using courseware can improve effects, but that\'s not an option. The options are about the effects of courseware, so perhaps the hypothesis is that using courseware can save time, which is D.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the hypothesis is that using courseware can have both advantages, but the options don\'t reflect that.\n\nWait, the question is: which statement is the hypothesis on which the above argument depends. So, the argument is that using courseware can improve teaching effects, and even if it\'s too simple, it can save time. So, the main hypothesis is that using courseware can improve teaching effects. But that\'s not an option. The options are about the effects of courseware.\n\nWait, perhaps the argument is structured as: Using courseware can save time (hypothesis), and even if it\'s too simple, it can improve effects. But that\'s not how it\'s written.\n\nWait, the context says: "There is no doubt that the use of multimedia courseware can improve the teaching effect." So, that\'s the main premise. Then it says, "Even if the courseware is too simple, only the traditional blackboard writing move, cannot really achieve the effect of multimedia, can also play a time-saving role." So, the argument is that using courseware can improve effects, and even if it\'s too simple, it can save time. So, the hypothesis is that using courseware can 