- Regardless of whether Y is on or off, T must be off.\n   - Y can be either on or off, but based on condition (4), if Y is on, W must be on, and X must be on. However, since S is on, T must be off.\n\n**Final Answer:**\n- **B)** Both T and Y are turned off.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
