scussion.\n\nSo, the options are A, B, C, D. The context already mentions all these aspects except maybe one.\n\nWait, the question is about what's least likely to be introduced next. So, perhaps the next part is about the treatment plan, which is already mentioned, so A is about breakthroughs, which is already covered.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the next part is about the contribution of traditional Chinese medicine, which is C.\n\nWait, I'm getting stuck. Let me try to think differently. The context says that the article mentions new progress in several areas, including causes of drug resistance, treatment, and lupus. It also mentions the treatment plan and contributions from traditional medicine.\n\nSo, the next part might be discussing the treatment plan, which is already mentioned, so perhaps the next part is about the causes or the unique effect.\n\nAlternatively, the next part might be about the contribution of traditional Chinese medicine, which is C.\n\nWait, but the context says that the contribution has been highly recognized, so maybe that's part of the next discussion.\n\nAlternatively, the next part might be about the unique effect of artemisinin in lupus, which is B.\n\nWait, I'm not making progress here. Let me try to think of the options again.\n\nOption A: New breakthrough in drug resistance research. The context says they've made new breakthroughs, so this is likely.\n\nOption B: Unique effect in lupus. Context mentions progress here, so likely.\n\nOption C: Contribution of traditional Chinese medicine. Context mentions this has been recognized, so likely.\n\nOption D: Cause of drug resistance. Context mentions this as part of their research, so likely.\n\nWait, but the question is about what's least likely to be introduced next. So, perhaps one of these is not part of the next discussion.\n\nWait, the context says that the article mentions a feasible treatment plan, new progress in lupus, and contributions from traditional medicine. So, the next par