reatment, lupus, and contributions. So, the next part might be about the treatment plan, which is already mentioned, so perhaps the next part is about the causes or the unique effect.\n\nAlternatively, the next part might be about the contribution of traditional Chinese medicine, which is C.\n\nWait, I think I'm overcomplicating this. Let me try to think of the options again.\n\nThe options are:.\n\nA) New breakthrough in drug resistance research.\n\nB) Unique effect in lupus.\n\nC) Contribution of traditional Chinese medicine.\n\nD) Cause of drug resistance.\n\nThe context says that the article mentions new breakthroughs in causes, treatment, lupus, and contributions. So, the next part might be about the treatment plan, which is part of the breakthroughs, so A is likely.\n\nAlternatively, the next part might be about the unique effect, which is B.\n\nWait, but the context says that new progress has been made in the treatment of lupus, so B is likely.\n\nAlternatively, the next part might be about the contribution of traditional Chinese medicine, which is C.\n\nWait, I'm not making progress. Let me try to think of the answer as D because the cause is already discussed, but the question is about the next part, so perhaps the next part is about the treatment plan or the unique effect.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the next part is about the contribution of traditional Chinese medicine, which is C.\n\nWait, I'm really stuck. I think I need to make a guess here. Based on the context, the next part is likely to discuss the causes, mechanisms, treatment, or contributions. Since the context already mentions the causes, the next part might be about the treatment plan or the unique effect.\n\nSo, the least likely would be the cause, D, because it's already mentioned. But the question is about the next part, so perhaps the next part is about the unique effect, B.\n\nWait, I'm not sure. I think I'll go with D as the least likely because the cause is already discussed, but the next