      "text": " C) Most of the workers who have earned the certificate are high school graduates.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nLet's analyze the given context and question step by step.\n\n**Context:**\n- **Most employees with a high school diploma have earned their factory safety certificate.**  \n  - This implies that a significant portion of high school graduates have successfully completed the training.\n- **High school graduates who haven't earned the certificate have evening obligations preventing them from taking the course.**  \n  - This suggests that some high school graduates are unable to complete the training due to personal commitments.\n- **Overall, most factory workers have not earned the certificate.**  \n  - This indicates that the majority of factory workers are either high school dropouts or have not completed the training for other reasons.\n\n**Question:**\n- Which statement must also be true based on the given information?\n\n**Options:**\n1. **A) A large proportion of the factory workers have not graduated from high school.**  \n   - This is supported by the statement that \"most factory workers have not earned the certificate.\" Since earning the certificate is tied to completing the training, which is available to high school graduates, a large proportion of factory workers not graduating from high school aligns with the context.\n\n2. **B) A large proportion of students with high school diplomas have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the eight-week training course.**  \n   - While some high school graduates have evening obligations, the context does not specify that this is true for a \"large proportion.\" It only mentions that those who haven't earned the certificate are due to such obligations. Therefore, this cannot be definitively concluded.\n\n3. **C) Most of the workers who have earned the certificate are high school graduates.**  \n   - This directly follows from the first statement in the context, which states that \"nearly all employees of the factory who have completed their high school diploma have earned their factory safety certificate.\" This clearly indicates that the majority of certificate holders are high school graduates.\n\n4. **D) No factory worker without a high school diploma has completed the course and earned the certificate.**  \n   - The context does not explicitly state that no factory worker without a high school diploma has earned the certificate. It only mentions that most factory workers have not earned the certificate, which could include both high school dropouts and those who couldn't complete the training for other reasons.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nBased on the context, **Option C** must be true.\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\boxed{C}",
