messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIn the process of accompanying their children, many parents will encounter the problem of their children lying or concealing the truth. Lying is almost what many parents are most worried about. Their children's bad behavior is even more frightening and angry than their children's poor academic performance.If we say that many parents have not solved the problem of their children lying well, at least most of them should pay attention to it, while the problem of children concealing their own situation from their parents is not only worse solved, but also not given enough attention.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is true of the original text?\n# Options:\nA) Parents think that children's failure to report information is more worrying than lying\nB) Parents believe that lying is the most unforgivable moral problem\nC) Most parents are more than willing to solve the problem of children lying\nD) Children's behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents", '<think>.\nOkay, so I need to figure out the correct answer to this logical reasoning question. Let me read through the context and the question carefully.\n\nThe context is about parents dealing with their children lying or concealing the truth. It mentions that lying is what many parents are most worried about. It also says that children\'s bad behavior is even more frustrating than poor academic performance. The context goes on to state that while many parents haven\'t solved the lying problem well, at least most pay attention to it. However, the problem of children concealing their own situations from their parents is worse and not given enough attention.\n\nNow, the question is asking which of the options A, B, C, or D is true based on the original text.\n\nLet me look at each option one by one.\n\nOption A: "Parents think that children\'s failure to report information is more worrying than lying." Hmm. The context says that lying is what parents are most worried about, and that children\'s bad behavior (which I assume includes lying) is more worrying than poor academic performance. It also mentions that failure to report (concealing) is worse but not given enough attention. So, does the text say that failure to report is more worrying than lying? I don\'t think so. It says lying is more worrying than poor academic performance, but it doesn\'t directly compare failure to report with lying. So maybe A is not correct.\n\nOption B: "Parents believe that lying is the most unforgivable moral problem." The context doesn\'t explicitly state that lying is the most unforgivable moral problem. It just says lying is what many parents are most worried about. So B might not be correct unless it\'s implied, but I don\'t see a direct statement.\n\nOption C: "Most parents are more than willing to solve the problem of children lying." The context says that while many parents haven\'t solved the lying problem well, at least most pay attention to it. So it suggests that most parents are aware of the problem but perhaps not effectively addressing it. The option says they are "more than willing" to solve it, which might not be directly supported. The context doesn\'t explicitly say they are willing; it just mentions they pay attention.\n\nOption D: "Children\'s behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents." The context says that the problem of children concealing their situation is not only worse but also not given enough attention. So this directly supports D being true.\n\nWait, let me double-check. The context says that while lying is a problem that most parents pay attention to, the problem of concealing is worse and not given enough attention</think>\n\nThe correct answer is D. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
