      "text": " B) Zhao is the heaviest.\n</think>\n\nLet's analyze the problem step by step.\n\n**Context:**\n1. Zhao, Qian, Sun, and Li compare their weights.\n2. It is known that Zhao and Qian's weight is equal to Sun and Li's weight.\n   - This implies: Zhao = Qian = Sun = Li\n3. When Qian and Li are exchanged:\n   - Zhao and Li's weight is higher than Qian and Sun's weight.\n   - Money's weight is greater than Zhao and Sun's weight.\n\n**Question:**\nBased on the above information, which of the following is true?\n\n**Options:**\nA) Qian is the heaviest.\nB) Zhao is the heaviest.\nC) Sun is the heaviest.\nD) Li is the heaviest.\n\n**Analysis:**\nFrom the context:\n- Initially, all four individuals (Zhao, Qian, Sun, Li) have equal weight.\n- After exchanging Qian and Li:\n  - Zhao and Li's combined weight is higher than Qian and Sun's combined weight.\n  - Money's weight is greater than Zhao and Sun's combined weight.\n\nThis implies that **Zhao** is the heaviest individual.\n\n**Answer:**\n\\boxed{B) Zhao is the heaviest.}",
