messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIn public speeches, some people talk long and talk endlessly; some people condense their meaning into one sentence, and this sentence is like a heavy stone, stirring up waves in the calm mind of the audience It is commendable and memorable. On October 19, 1936, at the meeting of people from all walks of life in Shanghai to sacrifice Lu Xun, my country's famous journalist, politician, and social activist Mr. Zou Taofen delivered a speech of only 33 words: Not too soon, I would like to commemorate Mr. with one sentence: Many people have fallen without a fight, and Mr. Lu Xun has fallen without a fight.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the main expression of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Short speeches, such as zou taofen's one-sentence speech, have profound meaning and strong expressive effects\nB) The phrase unyielding in battle accurately outlines mr. lu xun's fighting spirit\nC) The word war contains how much people admire and praise mr. lu xun\nD) Many shameless literati not only do not fight, but also slave their hands and knees; but the gentleman's eyebrows are cold and stubborn", '<think>.\nOkay, so I need to figure out the main expression of the given text. Let me read through the context again to make sure I understand it correctly.\n\nThe context talks about public speeches where some people give long, endless talks, while others condense their meaning into one sentence. It mentions that a one-sentence speech can be like a heavy stone, stirring waves in the audience\'s calm mind, making it commendable and memorable. Then, it gives an example: On October 19, 1936, Mr. Zou Taofen delivered a speech of only 33 words. The specific sentence he used was, "Many people have fallen without a fight, and Mr. Lu Xun has fallen without a fight.".\n\nThe question is asking which of the options A, B, C, or D is the main expression of this text. The options are:.\n\nA) Short speeches, such as zou taofen\'s one-sentence speech, have profound meaning and strong expressive effects.\n\nB) The phrase unyielding in battle accurately outlines mr. lu xun\'s fighting spirit.\n\nC) The word war contains how much people admire and praise mr. lu xun.\n\nD) Many shameless literati not only do not fight, but also slave their hands and knees; but the gentleman\'s eyebrows are cold and stubborn.\n\nFirst, I need to identify the key message in the context. It seems to be highlighting the effectiveness of concise speeches, using Mr. Zou Taofen\'s example. The speech is only 33 words, yet it\'s memorable and has a strong impact. So the main point is about the power of a single, well-crafted sentence.\n\nLooking at the options, option A talks about short speeches having profound meaning and strong expressive effects. That aligns with the idea that a single, impactful sentence can stir the audience. Option B refers to Mr. Lu Xun\'s fighting spirit, but the context doesn\'t explicitly mention his fighting spirit; it talks about his falling without a fight, which might imply something else. Option C mentions admiration and praise through the word "war," which doesn\'t seem directly related</think>.\n\nThe main expression of the text emphasizes the profound meaning and strong expressive effects of short, impactful speeches, such as Mr. Zou Taofen\'s one-sentence speech. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
