messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIn most cases, writing poems and filling words is a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion. It is unpredictable for a beginner to have what kind of feelings and choose what kind of sentence pattern to start with. But once he has a preliminary idea, he can always get appropriate help in the book Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms. He will know which words are suitable to express what kind of feelings, what kind of rhyme he should choose, and how to make rational use of certain rhetorical devices so as not to be fooled in the face of special syntax. If you have read enough ancient poems and have a certain sense of language, you will indeed be able to complete your first creation with the help of this book. It can not teach people to write amazing masterpieces, but with the greatest sincerity to prevent you from making all kinds of jokes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings is the main content of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Tang and song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones\nB) Poetry creation is essentially a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion\nC) Tang and song poetry rhythms provides a very good help for beginners\nD) The creator of poetry must have abundant emotion and high literary accomplishment', '<think>.\nOkay, so I need to figure out the main content of the given text. Let me read through the context again to understand it better.\n\nThe text starts by talking about writing poems and filling words as a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion. That means it\'s about how language and emotion influence each other in poetry. It\'s hard for a beginner to know what feelings to express or which sentence patterns to use at first. But then it mentions a book called "Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms" which helps them. The book tells them which words are suitable for expressing certain feelings, what rhymes to use, and how to use rhetorical devices without making syntax errors. It also says that if you\'ve read enough ancient poems and have a sense of language, you can use this book to complete your first creation. It\'s not about creating masterpieces, but about preventing mistakes.\n\nNow, looking at the question: Which option is the main content of the text?.\n\nThe options are A, B, C, D.\n\nOption A says Tang and Song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones. The context does mention the book helps beginners, but it\'s more about structure and emotion guidance, not specifically rich tones.\n\nOption B states that poetry creation is a mutual accommodation between language and emotion. The text starts by saying that writing poems is a process of mutual accommodation, so this seems to be the main point.\n\nOption C says the book provides very good help for beginners. The context does talk about the book helping, but it\'s more about the process of creation and the book\'s role, not just the help itself.\n\nOption D says the creator must have abundant emotion and high literary accomplishment. The text doesn\'t mention anything about the creator\'s emotions or accomplishments, so this isn\'t supported.\n\nSo, the main content is about the process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion in poetry creation</think>.\n\nThe main content of the text is about the process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion in poetry creation. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
