      "text": "4) Can not implement absolute fairness.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is D) Can not implement absolute fairness.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Understanding the Context:**\n   - If absolute fairness (A) is implemented, it leads to distribution according to work (B).\n   - Distribution according to work (B) results in inequality (D).\n   - To implement absolute fairness (A), equality between the rich and poor (C) is necessary.\n\n2. **Logical Implications:**\n   - From A \u2192 B and B \u2192 D, we get A \u2192 D (absolute fairness leads to inequality).\n   - However, A also requires C (equality), leading to a contradiction because A cannot both lead to D (inequality) and C (equality).\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\n   - The contradiction implies that absolute fairness cannot be implemented.\n\n**Answer:** D) Can not implement absolute fairness.",
