messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nZhao Ming, Qian Hong and Sun Jie were admitted to Peking University, Tsinghua University and Beijing normal University. About which school they were admitted to, the students made the following guesses: classmate A guessed: Zhao Ming was admitted by Tsinghua University and Sun Jie was admitted by Beijing normal University. Classmate B guess: Zhao Ming was admitted by Beijing normal University and Qian Hong was admitted by Tsinghua University. Classmate C guess: Zhao Ming was admitted to Peking University and Sun Jie was admitted to Tsinghua University. As a result, the students' guesses were half right.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is their correct admission?\n# Options:\nA) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to peking university, tsinghua university and beijing normal university respectively.\nB) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to tsinghua university, beijing normal university and peking university respectively.\nC) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to beijing normal university, tsinghua university and peking university respectively.\nD) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to peking university, beijing normal university and tsinghua university respectively.", '<think>.\nOkay, so I have this logic problem to solve, and I need to figure out the correct answer based on the given context. Let me try to break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, let\'s read the context carefully. There are three students: Zhao Ming, Qian Hong, and Sun Jie. They were admitted to three different universities: Peking University, Tsinghua University, and Beijing Normal University. Each of them made guesses about where their classmates were admitted.\n\nClassmate A guessed that Zhao Ming was admitted to Tsinghua University and Sun Jie was admitted to Beijing Normal University. So, according to A, Zhao Ming → Tsinghua, Sun Jie → Beijing Normal.\n\nClassmate B guessed that Zhao Ming was admitted to Beijing Normal University and Qian Hong was admitted to Tsinghua University. So, B\'s guesses are Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal, Qian Hong → Tsinghua.\n\nClassmate C guessed that Zhao Ming was admitted to Peking University and Sun Jie was admitted to Tsinghua University. So, C says Zhao Ming → Peking, Sun Jie → Tsinghua.\n\nThe result is that the students\' guesses were half right. So, out of the three guesses each made, only one was correct, and the other two were wrong. Wait, no, actually, the total number of correct guesses across all classmates is half right. Since each classmate made two guesses, and there are three classmates, that\'s a total of six guesses. Half right would mean three correct and three incorrect.\n\nBut wait, the problem says "the students\' guesses were half right." So, perhaps each student\'s two guesses had one correct and one incorrect. That would make sense because each of them made two guesses, so each got one right and one wrong. So, three students, each with one correct guess, totaling three correct and three incorrect across all guesses.\n\nNow, the question is asking which option correctly lists their admissions. The options are A, B, C, D, each listing the three students with the universities they were admitted to.\n\nLet me list out each option and see how many correct guesses they would result in.\n\nOption A: Zhao Ming → Peking, Qian Hong → Tsinghua, Sun Jie → Beijing Normal.\n\nLet\'s check each guess against the options.\n\nFirst, check Classmate A\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Tsinghua (A says Tsinghua, but in Option A, Zhao Ming is at Peking. So A\'s first guess is wrong. Sun Jie → Beijing Normal (A says Beijing Normal, which matches Option A. So A has one correct (Sun Jie) and one wrong (Zhao Ming).\n\nClassmate B\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal (B says Beijing Normal, but in Option A, Zhao Ming is at Peking. So wrong. Qian Hong → Tsinghua (B says Tsinghua, which matches Option A. So B has one correct (Qian Hong) and one wrong (Zhao Ming).\n\nClassmate C\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Peking (C says Peking, which matches Option A. So correct. Sun Jie → Tsinghua (C says Tsinghua, but in Option A, Sun Jie is at Beijing Normal. So wrong. So C has one correct (Zhao Ming) and one wrong (Sun Jie).\n\nSo total correct guesses: A (Sun Jie), B (Qian Hong), C (Zhao Ming). That\'s three correct, which is half right as per the context. So Option A is possible.\n\nOption B: Zhao Ming → Tsinghua, Qian Hong → Beijing Normal, Sun Jie → Peking.\n\nCheck each guess.\n\nClassmate A: Zhao Ming → Tsinghua (A says Tsinghua, which matches. Correct. Sun Jie → Beijing Normal (A says Beijing Normal, but in Option B, Sun Jie is at Peking. So wrong. So A has one correct, one wrong.\n\nClassmate B: Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal (B says Beijing Normal, but in Option B, Zhao Ming is at Tsinghua. Wrong. Qian Hong → Tsinghua (B says Tsinghua, but in Option B, Qian Hong is at Beijing Normal. Wrong. So B has zero correct, which can\'t be because the total should be three correct. So Option B is out.\n\nOption C: Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal, Qian Hong → Peking, Sun Jie → Tsinghua.\n\nCheck each guess.\n\nClassmate A: Zhao Ming → Tsinghua (A says Tsinghua, but in Option C, Zhao Ming is at Beijing Normal. Wrong. Sun Jie → Beijing Normal (A says Beijing Normal, but in Option C, Sun Jie is at Tsinghua. Wrong. So A has zero correct. Not possible.\n\nOption D: Zhao Ming → Peking, Qian Hong → Beijing Normal, Sun Jie → Tsinghua.\n\nCheck each guess.\n\nClassmate A: Zhao Ming → Tsinghua (A says Tsinghua, but in D, Zhao Ming is at Peking. Wrong. Sun Jie → Beijing Normal (A says Beijing Normal, but in D, Sun Jie is at Tsinghua. Wrong. So A has zero correct. Not possible.\n\nWait, but let me double-check. Maybe I made a mistake.\n\nWait, in Option D: Zhao Ming → Peking, Qian Hong → Beijing Normal, Sun Jie → Tsinghua.\n\nSo, let\'s check each classmate\'s guesses.\n\nClassmate A: Zhao Ming → Tsinghua (wrong, he\'s at Peking). Sun Jie → Beijing Normal (wrong, she\'s at Tsinghua). So A has zero correct.\n\nClassmate B: Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal (wrong, he\'s at Peking). Qian Hong → Tsinghua (wrong, she\'s at Beijing Normal). So B has zero correct.\n\nClassmate C: Zhao Ming → Peking (correct). Sun Jie → Tsinghua (correct). So C has two correct. But the total correct should be three, so this can\'t be because C alone has two correct, and the others have zero, making total two correct, which is less than half. So Option D is out.\n\nWait, but earlier when I checked Option A, it resulted in three correct guesses, which fits the half right condition. So Option A is the correct answer.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I didn\'t miss anything. Let me go through each option again.\n\nOption A: Zhao Ming → Peking, Qian Hong → Tsinghua, Sun Jie → Beijing Normal.\n\nCheck each guess:.\n\nA\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Tsinghua (wrong), Sun Jie → Beijing Normal (correct). So A has one correct.\n\nB\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal (wrong), Qian Hong → Tsinghua (correct). So B has one correct.\n\nC\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Peking (correct), Sun Jie → Tsinghua (wrong). So C has one correct.\n\nTotal correct: 3. That\'s half right because there are six guesses in total (three students, two each), so 3 correct and 3 incorrect. So Option A fits.\n\nOption B: Zhao Ming → Tsinghua, Qian Hong → Beijing Normal, Sun Jie → Peking.\n\nCheck each guess:.\n\nA\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Tsinghua (correct), Sun Jie → Beijing Normal (wrong). So A has one correct.\n\nB\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal (wrong), Qian Hong → Tsinghua (wrong). So B has zero correct.\n\nC\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Peking (wrong), Sun Jie → Tsinghua (wrong). So C has zero correct.\n\nTotal correct: 1. That\'s way below half, so Option B is out.\n\nOption C: Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal, Qian Hong → Peking, Sun Jie → Tsinghua.\n\nCheck each guess:.\n\nA\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Tsinghua (wrong), Sun Jie → Beijing Normal (wrong). So A has zero.\n\nB\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal (correct), Qian Hong → Tsinghua (wrong). So B has one.\n\nC\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Peking (wrong), Sun Jie → Tsinghua (correct). So C has one.\n\nTotal correct: 2. Still not half, so Option C is out.\n\nOption D: Zhao Ming → Peking, Qian Hong → Beijing Normal, Sun Jie → Tsinghua.\n\nCheck each guess:.\n\nA\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Tsinghua (wrong), Sun Jie → Beijing Normal (wrong). So A has zero.\n\nB\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal (wrong), Qian Hong → Tsinghua (wrong). So B has zero.\n\nC\'s guesses: Zhao Ming → Peking (correct), Sun Jie → Tsinghua (correct). So C has two.\n\nTotal correct: 2. Again, not half, so Option D is out</think>.\n\nThe correct answer is A.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**.\n\n1. **Understand the Context:**.\n   - Three students (Zhao Ming, Qian Hong, Sun Jie) were admitted to three universities (Peking, Tsinghua, Beijing Normal).\n   - Each student made two guesses about their classmates\' admissions.\n   - The total number of correct guesses across all students is half (i.e., 3 correct out of 6 guesses).\n\n2. **Analyze Each Option:**.\n   - **Option A:** Zhao Ming → Peking, Qian Hong → Tsinghua, Sun Jie → Beijing Normal.\n     - **Classmate A\'s Guesses:** Zhao Ming (wrong), Sun Jie (correct) → 1 correct.\n     - **Classmate B\'s Guesses:** Zhao Ming (wrong), Qian Hong (correct) → 1 correct.\n     - **Classmate C\'s Guesses:** Zhao Ming (correct), Sun Jie (wrong) → 1 correct.\n     - **Total Correct:** 3 (meets the half-right condition).\n\n   - **Option B:** Zhao Ming → Tsinghua, Qian Hong → Beijing Normal, Sun Jie → Peking.\n     - **Classmate A\'s Guesses:** Zhao Ming (correct), Sun Jie (wrong) → 1 correct.\n     - **Classmate B\'s Guesses:** Both wrong → 0 correct.\n     - **Classmate C\'s Guesses:** Both wrong → 0 correct.\n     - **Total Correct:** 1 (does not meet the condition).\n\n   - **Option C:** Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal, Qian Hong → Peking, Sun Jie → Tsinghua.\n     - **Classmate A\'s Guesses:** Both wrong → 0 correct.\n     - **Classmate B\'s Guesses:** Zhao Ming (correct), Qian Hong (wrong) → 1 correct.\n     - **Classmate C\'s Guesses:** Zhao Ming (wrong), Sun Jie (correct) → 1 correct.\n     - **Total Correct:** 2 (does not meet the condition).\n\n   - **Option D:** Zhao Ming → Peking, Qian Hong → Beijing Normal, Sun Jie → Tsinghua.\n     - **Classmate A\'s Guesses:** Both wrong → 0 correct.\n     - **Classmate B\'s Guesses:** Both wrong → 0 correct.\n     - **Classmate C\'s Guesses:** Both correct → 2 correct.\n     - **Total Correct:** 2 (does not meet the condition).\n\n3. **Conclusion:**. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 82%|########2 | 494/600 [11:40<01:33,  1.13it/s]
