      "text": " A) Wang Ming and Li Zilu didn't tick each other.\n</think>\n\nLet's analyze the problem step by step.\n\n**Context:**\n1. **Voting Mechanism:** All staff members of the Bureau are to vote for the head of the personnel section. Each staff member can tick the list of employees they support.\n2. **Candidates:** The top three candidates are Zhang Hao, Wang Ming, and Li Zilu.\n3. **Vote Counting Findings:**\n   - **Zhang Hao** did not tick anyone.\n   - **Wang Ming** checked all those who checked **Zhao Jie**.\n   - **Li Zilu** ticked all those who did not get the full vote.\n\n**Question:** Based on the above information, which of the following is true?\n\n**Options:**\n- **A)** Wang Ming and Li Zilu didn't tick each other.\n- **B)** Wang Ming and Li Zilu tick each other.\n- **C)** Wang Ming chose Li Zilu, but Li Zilu didn't choose Wang Ming.\n- **D)** Wang Ming didn't choose Li Zilu, but Li Zilu chose Wang Ming.\n\n**Analysis:**\n- **Zhang Hao** did not tick anyone, so he did not support any candidate.\n- **Wang Ming** checked all those who checked **Zhao Jie**. This implies that Wang Ming supported everyone who supported Zhao Jie.\n- **Li Zilu** ticked all those who did not get the full vote. This means Li Zilu supported candidates who did not receive votes from everyone.\n\n**Interpretation:**\n- Since Zhang Hao did not tick anyone, he did not support any candidate.\n- Wang Ming supported all those who supported Zhao Jie, but there is no information that Wang Ming was supported by anyone else.\n- Li Zilu supported candidates who did not receive full votes, which could include Wang Ming if Wang Ming did not receive votes from everyone.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n- **Wang Ming** did not tick **Li Zilu**, but **Li Zilu** ticked **Wang Ming** because Wang Ming did not receive the full vote.\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\boxed{D) Wang Ming didn't choose Li Zilu, but Li Zilu chose Wang Ming}",
